# CRAP Metric Hotspots

Read [`.agents/skills/complexity-lcov-join/SKILL.md`](../../skills/complexity-lcov-join/SKILL.md) before changing Rust complexity, merge, or LCOV parse files.

Read [`.agents/skills/complexity-go/SKILL.md`](../../skills/complexity-go/SKILL.md) before changing `crap-go` complexity, coverprofile, or build tags.

Read [`.agents/skills/complexity-ts/SKILL.md`](../../skills/complexity-ts/SKILL.md) before changing `crap-ts` complexity, walk, or project resolve.

- Cognitive `match` is one nesting-weighted increment, not one per arm (Rust).
- Closures fold into the enclosing function; nested `fn` / named funcs are separate rows.
- Empty instrumented spans use `--missing` (default 0%). Do not treat them as 100%.
- `MatchRank` prefers forward path matches over reverse suffix length.
- Coverprofile parsing stays in `crap-go`; do not add it to `crap-core`.
- Istanbul / V8 JSON stays out of `crap-core`; `crap-ts` uses on-disk LCOV.